From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ARM: configs: gts28ltexx: FAT, exFAT and their code pages
 for the microSD card

Cards come formatted FAT32 (SDHC, up to 32 GB) or exFAT (SDXC); the
board had neither file system.  Build in vfat (UTF-8 names by default)
and exfat, with the code pages their mount options ask for: 437,
vfat's default codepage, iso8859-1, its default iocharset, and utf8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
index e3adeca5d..ed177b8bd 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
@@ -129,6 +129,18 @@ CONFIG_AUTOFS_FS=y
 CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
 CONFIG_TMPFS=y
 CONFIG_TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y
+
+# The microSD slot (mshc_2, the board DTS's section 7): cards come
+# formatted FAT32 (SDHC, up to 32 GB) or exFAT (SDXC), so both are built
+# in, with the code pages the mount options ask for (vfat's default
+# codepage 437, utf8 for the names) and iso8859-1, vfat's default
+# iocharset.
+CONFIG_VFAT_FS=y
+CONFIG_FAT_DEFAULT_UTF8=y
+CONFIG_EXFAT_FS=y
+CONFIG_NLS_CODEPAGE_437=y
+CONFIG_NLS_ISO8859_1=y
+CONFIG_NLS_UTF8=y
 CONFIG_PSTORE=y
 CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
 CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG=y
-- 
